>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `MODEL_REFUTE_TAC`

``` hol4
Refute.MODEL_REFUTE_TAC : tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Searches for a counterexample with the finite model finder.

`MODEL_REFUTE_TAC` is `REFUTE_TAC_WITH [upd_search (Only [ModelFinder])]`:
it runs the `kodkod` backend, which needs the external Kodkodi
component; without it the result is `Unknown`.  With the `falsify`
field false it searches for a model of the goal and reports `Model`
or `NoModel`.  `model_refute` (see `Refute.refute`) is the
corresponding function on terms.

### Failure

Fails only if the configuration's `expect` field is not met.

### Comments

The model finder reads only the equations a user wrote.  The `ARB`
case HOL4 adds to a non-exhaustive definition is unconstrained, so a
goal true only because of it can get a counterexample, as in Isabelle's
Nitpick.

